## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical RN UI layering, cross-platform overlays, and accessibility basics for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Overlay rendering, singleton manager, message queue
- Accessibility (aria-live/polite) and reduced motion
- Theming and platform-agnostic styling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo sketch of ToastProvider + showToast API
import React, {createContext, useContext, useState} from 'react';
export const ToastContext = createContext({showToast: ()=>{}, hideToast: ()=>{}});
export function ToastProvider({children}) {
  const [toast, setToast] = useState(null);
  const showToast = (message, {duration=2000, position='bottom'} = {}) => {
    setToast({message, duration, position});
    // queue logic omitted for brevity
  };
  // render overlay with message, dismiss after duration
  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{showToast, hideToast}}>
      {children}
      {toast && (
        <div role="status" aria-live="polite">{toast.message}</div>
      )}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
}
```

